> [!IMPORTANT]
> **App link: <https://g-c-3.github.io/drivefiles/>**
> Open it on your phone, tablet or computer. Everything runs in your browser; there is no server.

---

## What it is

**Atlas** is a single-page file manager for one GitHub repository. It runs entirely in your browser from GitHub Pages and talks to GitHub directly with your own access token. Use it to:

- browse, select, copy, move, rename, delete and download the repository's files and folders,
- upload files into any folder,
- **extract archives straight into a folder** (ZIP, 7z, RAR, TAR, GZ, BZ2, XZ and more), including password-protected ones,
- download any selection as one **zip, with or without a password**,
- undo the latest change from History.

It adapts to phones, foldables, tablets and desktops: bottom tabs on narrow screens, a sidebar with a folder tree from about 640 px, and a windowed layout on large screens. Light and dark themes follow your device, and animations respect "reduce motion".

## Quick start

1. Create a **fine-grained personal access token** at GitHub → Settings → Developer settings → Personal access tokens. Select only the repository `drivefiles` and grant **Contents: Read and write**.
2. Open **<https://g-c-3.github.io/drivefiles/>**.
3. Fill in:

   | Field | Example |
   |---|---|
   | GitHub Account Name | `g-c-3` |
   | Repo Name | `drivefiles` |
   | Branch (optional) | `main` |
   | Read & Write Access Token | `github_pat_…` |
   | Passcode (recommended) | your own |

4. Tap **Continue**. The first screen is the file manager for your repo.

> [!NOTE]
> With a passcode, your details are stored on **this device only**, encrypted (PBKDF2-SHA256, 200,000 rounds, AES-256-GCM). Next time you just enter the passcode. Without a passcode nothing is saved.

## The three tabs

### Files
- Tap a folder to open it, tick checkboxes (or **Select all**) to pick items.
- The action bar appears with **Download · Copy · Move · Rename · Delete**.
- **Add files** uploads to the current folder; **Change** opens a file-manager style folder picker where you can also create folders.
- **New folder** creates a folder (Git has no empty folders, so a hidden `.gitkeep` is added and never shown).
- Search matches file and folder names anywhere in the repo.

### Extract
1. Drop or choose one or more archives.
2. If an archive is locked, a **Password needed** card appears. Enter the password and tap **Unlock**.
3. Tick the folders or files you want. Large files are held back (see limits).
4. Pick the destination folder with the picker, choose how to handle duplicates, tap **Extract selected**.

Progress is committed in batches, so if the connection drops you can run it again and finished files are skipped.

### History
Every change is a Git commit. **Undo this change** on the newest entry restores the previous state (the undo is itself a commit, so you can undo it too).

## Supported archives

| Format | Open | Password |
|---|---|---|
| ZIP (ZipCrypto and AES-128/192/256) | ✅ | ✅ |
| 7z (including encrypted file names) | ✅ | ✅ |
| TAR, TAR.GZ / TGZ, TAR.BZ2, TAR.XZ | ✅ | n/a |
| GZ, BZ2, XZ (single file) | ✅ | n/a |
| RAR | ✅ via 7-Zip's RAR support | ✅ |
| Others 7-Zip reads (ISO, CAB, WIM, …) | ✅ | where the format has one |

> [!NOTE]
> ZIP, 7z, TAR, GZ, BZ2 and XZ were tested end to end. RAR support comes from the bundled 7-Zip engine but I had no RAR sample to test with, so treat it as untested.

## Downloading

- One file: downloads directly.
- Several items or a folder: packed into one `.zip` in your browser. Optionally set a **password**:
  - **Strong (AES-256)**: opens in 7-Zip, WinZip, and most Android apps.
  - **Compatible (ZipCrypto)**: opens almost everywhere, but is much weaker.

## When a file already exists

| File option | Result |
|---|---|
| **Skip** | Leave the existing file alone |
| **Keep both** | Save the new one as `name_1`, `name_2`, … (identical files are detected and not duplicated) |
| **Replace** | Overwrite (undo from History) |

| Folder option | Result |
|---|---|
| **Merge** | Put new files into the existing folder |
| **Save as copy** | Save the folder as `Folder_1`, `Folder_2`, … |

## Limits worth knowing

- **100 MB** per file is GitHub's hard limit through this route; larger files are marked and can't be sent.
- Files above **48 MB** (adjustable) are held back by default so you can opt in one by one.
- Everything is processed in memory. Very large archives (hundreds of MB) can fail on a phone; split them or use a computer.
- GitHub rate-limits writes. The app paces itself and waits when asked.
- Keep the tab open and the screen on while a long job runs.

## Privacy and security

- No server, analytics or third-party requests. The page only talks to `api.github.com`.
- Your token is used only in requests to GitHub. Use a fine-grained token limited to this one repo, and revoke it if a device is lost.
- This page is public because Pages is public, but it contains no secrets. Strangers see only the setup form and can't see your files without a token.
- **Lock** and **Forget this device** are in the menu (⋯). The app also locks after two minutes in the background.

## Troubleshooting

| Message | Fix |
|---|---|
| Token was rejected | Edit details and paste a valid token |
| Repository or branch not found | Check the account, repo and branch spelling, and that the token covers this repo |
| No permission | The token needs **Contents: Read and write** |
| Repository is empty | Add one file in GitHub (for example a README) first |
| Password didn't work | Check case and spaces; names can be encrypted in 7z |
| Extraction fails on a big archive | Close other tabs, or use a computer |

## Notes on layout

The layout is responsive and works on foldable phones in both folded and unfolded widths. It does not read the hinge position, so it will not split around the fold.

## Credits and licences

- [**7-Zip**](https://www.7-zip.org/) compiled to WebAssembly in the [`7z-wasm`](https://www.npmjs.com/package/7z-wasm) package (7-Zip 24.09): LGPL, with the **unRAR restriction** (the RAR code may not be used to recreate the RAR compression algorithm).
- [**zip.js**](https://gildas-lormeau.github.io/zip.js/) 2.25.0: BSD-3-Clause.

Both are bundled into the single `index.html`, so the app needs no other files.

## Deploying

Put `index.html` in the repository root, then Settings → Pages → *Deploy from a branch* → `main` / root. The app is then served at `https://g-c-3.github.io/drivefiles/`.
